# Kit maintainer (this repo only)

This file is **not** `crav1-*` so a folder dump of the library can omit it. Product repos get `.cursor/rules/crav1.mdc` (Cursor) or `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (Claude Code), not this file.

This repo’s custom library uses the **`crav1`** prefix so it is distinct from Cursor built-ins. Skill and agent names stay the same on Claude Code.

There are **three install trees**. Cursor drop-in `.cursor/` is the source of the playbooks. `plugins/crav1/` is the Cursor plugin mirror. `.claude/` is the generated Claude Code drop-in. When you add or change a skill, agent, template, or kit rule, edit `.cursor/` and run `scripts/sync-crav1-plugin.sh`. That refreshes the plugin mirror and regenerates `.claude/`. Do not hand-edit mirrored files under `plugins/crav1/` or anything under `.claude/`. Also update `docs/install.md` and `plugins/crav1/README.md` when how people install or start using the kit changes.

CI (`.github/workflows/drop-in-plugin-sync.yml`) fails the check when the plugin mirror drifts, and when `scripts/sync-crav1-claude.sh --check` exits non-zero because the committed `.claude/` tree does not match a fresh generate. A comment in this rule is not the check.

## Drop-in (project `.cursor/`)

- Skills: `.cursor/skills/crav1/crav1-<short-name>/` with frontmatter `name: crav1-<short-name>` (must match the folder that contains `SKILL.md`). Slash command: `/crav1-<short-name>`. Type `/crav1` to list them.
- Cross-cutting pull-request skills: `/crav1-open-pr` opens one pull request and does not merge. `/crav1-merge-pr` merges one named pull request only when the user explicitly asks in that turn, and only with a merge commit. Do not fold merge into open-pr, complete-task, or review skills.
- Agents: `.cursor/agents/crav1-<name>.md` with `name: crav1-<name>`. Subagent `name:` ends in `-agent` so the Cursor slash picker can tell them apart from skills that share the same stem (`/crav1-architecture-reviewer` stays the skill; `crav1-architecture-reviewer-agent` is the subagent).
- Guild routing: when you add, rename, or remove a skill, agent, or cross-cutting helper, update `docs/guild-routing.md` in the same PR. Update the behavior map in this file in that same PR.
- Agent templates: `.cursor/agent-assets/crav1-<name>/` (not under `.cursor/agents/`).
- Usage rule for consuming repos: `.cursor/rules/crav1.mdc`.

Do not add unprefixed copies at `.cursor/skills/<short-name>/` (name collision).

## Plugin mirror (`plugins/crav1/`)

Cursor plugin layout (install-from-repo / local plugin):

- Manifest: `plugins/crav1/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`
- Catalog: `.cursor-plugin/marketplace.json` (repo root)
- Skills: `plugins/crav1/skills/crav1-<short-name>/` (same `name:` and `SKILL.md` as drop-in)
- Agents: `plugins/crav1/agents/crav1-<name>.md`
- Agent templates: `plugins/crav1/agent-assets/crav1-<name>/`
- Rules: `plugins/crav1/rules/` (includes `crav1.mdc`; do not put this maintainer file in the plugin)

After editing drop-in files, run `scripts/sync-crav1-plugin.sh` so the plugin tree and `.claude/` match. Do not hand-edit mirrored files only under `plugins/crav1/` or `.claude/` — they will be overwritten. Plugin-only files: `plugins/crav1/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`, `plugins/crav1/README.md`. There is no Claude Code plugin marketplace in this kit.

## Claude Code drop-in (generated `.claude/`)

`scripts/sync-crav1-plugin.sh` calls `scripts/sync-crav1-claude.sh`, which writes `.claude/` from `.cursor/`. `scripts/sync-crav1-claude.sh --check` diffs a fresh generate against the committed tree and exits non-zero on drift. The same check runs in CI.

Path rewrite only: `.cursor/skills/crav1/<name>/` → `.claude/skills/<name>/`, `.cursor/agents/` → `.claude/agents/`, `.cursor/agent-assets/` → `.claude/agent-assets/`. Commit-style rules rewrite `.cursor/rules/draft-commit-*.mdc` to `.claude/rules/draft-commit-*.md`. The source skill text names Cursor and Claude Code; the generator rewrites the Cursor paths in the Claude copy.

Hand-written host differences inside that generator, not a second copy of every `SKILL.md`:

- Agent frontmatter. `model: inherit` is omitted (Claude Code’s default). `readonly: true` becomes `tools: Read, Grep, Glob`. Writers omit `tools` so they can edit.
- `.cursor/rules/crav1.mdc` becomes `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (the short project instruction, not the README).
- Commit-style assets drop Cursor `alwaysApply` frontmatter so `.claude/rules/*.md` loads at session start.

`.claude/agent-assets/` is not a directory Claude Code loads on its own. Prompts read those files. Do not put them under `.claude/agents/` (that tree is scanned as subagents). Do not copy this maintainer file into `.claude/`.

## Self-contained templates

When you **create or update** a crav1 skill or subagent that reads or writes spec artifacts (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `adr.md`, `diagrams.md`, `verify.md`, `fix-log.md`) or landscape artifacts (`docs/system/`):

1. Put a copy of each template in **that skill’s** `assets/` (and the matching `agent-assets/crav1-<agent-name>/` on both trees).
2. Point the `SKILL.md` / agent prompt at **those** copies, not only `docs/specs/_template/`. Mention drop-in `.cursor/…` **and** plugin sibling paths when a file lives outside this skill. The Claude generator rewrites the `.cursor/` paths.
3. Keep `docs/specs/_template/` and `docs/system/_template/` in sync with the matching `assets/` copies. If you change a template, update **every** copy.
4. Do **not** put template markdown under `.cursor/agents/` or `plugins/crav1/agents/` except the agent prompt file.
5. Format recipes live in the skill’s `references/` (see `crav1-export-spec` / `crav1-ideas-to-spec`).

Skills that do not use those files do not need empty `assets/` folders.

Optional Azure Boards id file: `docs/specs/_template/work-item.md` is the HTML-comment starter only. Do not copy that template into skill `assets/`, and do not copy the comment into a slug. Commit and pull-request skills read `docs/specs/<slug>/work-item.md` when it exists. `/crav1-spark-to-spec`, `/crav1-ideas-to-spec`, and `/crav1-intake-to-specs` may write the one-line file when the user opts in on Azure Repos (`crav1-draft-commit-message` `references/work-item-offer.md`). They do not write the file when the user skips.

## Install docs

Pre-install: `docs/install.md`. Post-plugin-install: `plugins/crav1/README.md`. Kit playbook: `README.md`, `docs/from-nothing.md`, `docs/from-ideas.md`, `docs/from-intake.md`.

## Behavior map

This map covers main. Read it before answering how a skill behaves. Lane ownership stays in `docs/guild-routing.md`. One line per skill: what it reads, what it writes, what it leaves alone, who calls it, and which skill or agent it calls. A second line is a real exception. An agent is listed only when it runs a skill. Naming a next command is not a call.

Starter options, when the user asks for startup options: `/crav1-spark-to-spec`, `/crav1-ideas-to-spec`, `/crav1-intake-to-specs`, `/crav1-match-to-specs`, `/crav1-repos-to-spec`, `/crav1-environment-read`, and `/crav1-fix-bug`. That ask names the list. It does not run a skill and does not move work into a lane. Every other skill is a later skill. Each starter still follows the rules it already has.

- `/crav1-spark-to-spec` — Reads the spark and the repo. Writes `docs/specs/<slug>/spec.md`, a thin `docs/system/` including `glossary.md` when that folder is missing, otherwise one index row plus a missing glossary or new glossary rows, and `work-item.md` when the user opts in on Azure Repos. Leaves application code and an existing landscape alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` when the repo already has commits.
  Exception: extend edits that spec and adds no second index row.
- `/crav1-ideas-to-spec` — Reads one unstructured pile and the repo. Writes `spec.md`, `diagrams.md`, slice ADRs, the chosen `export/`, optional `notes.md`, the same landscape or index-and-glossary result as spark, and `work-item.md` on an Azure Repos opt-in. Leaves application code and an existing landscape alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` when the repo already has commits.
  Exception: two or more v0 slices or repos writes nothing and points at `/crav1-intake-to-specs`.
- `/crav1-intake-to-specs` — Reads the intake files. Writes `docs/system/` including `glossary.md` (a missing glossary and new rows when the folder already exists), one `docs/specs/<slug>/` per confirmed v0 feature, the landscape index, and `work-item.md` on an Azure Repos opt-in. Leaves application code, `plan.md`, and later slices alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` when the repo already has commits.
  Exception: prompts `/crav1-finalize-commit` and does not run it.
- `/crav1-match-to-specs` — Reads the repos and the dump. Writes `docs/system/` in the destination the user picks (gaps only when it exists, including a missing glossary and new rows) and one `docs/specs/<slug>/spec.md` per confirmed slice, including not in the code, then index rows. Leaves application code, `plan.md`, `work-item.md`, and the rest of an existing landscape alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` in that destination when it already has commits.
  Exception: a slice that is not in the code stays thin and is not planned here.
- `/crav1-match-dump-to-specs` — Reads the dump and existing spec folders, skipping `_template`. Writes confirmed new quotes into the matching `spec.md` files, and a missing `glossary.md` or new glossary rows only when `docs/system/` already exists. Leaves leftovers, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and other landscape files alone unless the user picks apply. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: creates no slug and seeds no `docs/system/`.
- `/crav1-code-into-specs` — Reads a named commit, range, or branch diff, and existing spec folders. Writes quotes of what belongs into the matching `spec.md` files, and the same glossary gap as match-dump. Leaves leftovers, application code, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and other landscape files alone unless the user picks apply. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: creates no slug, seeds no `docs/system/`, and does not watch the repo.
- `/crav1-add-to-spec` — Reads the new information and one existing `spec.md`. Writes quotes into that file, and listed edits to `docs/system/` or another spec only when the user picks apply, including a new row on an existing glossary. Leaves `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and a missing `glossary.md` alone. Called by the user, by `/crav1-environment-read` for a confirmed Match section, by `/crav1-suggest-tests-for-code` for one kept or dismissed suggestion, and by `/crav1-meeting-to-specs` for one kept addition. Calls no skill.
  Exception: creates no slug and no `docs/system/`.
- `/crav1-architecture-reviewer` — Reads `spec.md`, `diagrams.md`, `adr/`, and `export/` when those exist. Writes nothing. Leaves the spec and code alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: the parent delegates the critique and does not review in its own voice. It names `/crav1-tighten-spec` and `/crav1-security-review` and does not run them.
- `/crav1-tighten-spec` — Reads `spec.md`, diagrams, ADRs, and reviewer findings already in the chat. Writes only the picked issue in `spec.md` and, when that pick says so, the named diagram, ADR, or export. Leaves application code and unpicked issues alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: `suggest` does not patch.
- `/crav1-resolve-questions` — Reads Open questions and unresolved assumptions in `spec.md`. Writes only the picked question into the spec, a constraint, a non-goal, or an ADR. Leaves application code and kept-open questions alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
- `/crav1-plan-from-spec` — Reads the accepted spec, diagrams, ADRs, exports, and kept security findings already written. Writes `plan.md` and `tasks.md`, and matching OpenSpec export files when those already exist. Leaves `spec.md`, application code, and any linter install alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: when `## Linter` says this repo has no linter for the code the tasks will touch, it stops before Build until the user chooses. A line under `## Dismissed test suggestions` is not a task. A kept test suggestion that is already an acceptance line maps to a task.
- `/crav1-review-plan` — Reads `spec.md`, `plan.md`, and `tasks.md`. Writes nothing. Leaves the plan and code alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: the parent delegates the critique and does not review in its own voice. It names `/crav1-tighten-plan` and does not run it.
- `/crav1-tighten-plan` — Reads `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `spec.md`, and plan-review findings already in the chat. Writes only the picked plan issue in `plan.md` or `tasks.md`. Leaves `spec.md` and application code alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: a spec-tagged finding is not patched here.
- `/crav1-implement-task` — Reads one `T#` in `tasks.md`, plus `plan.md` and `spec.md`. Writes the code and the checks that row names, and marks the row `[x]` only when that verify passes. Leaves `spec.md` and other tasks alone. Called by the user and by `crav1-complete-task-agent`. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` before code.
  Exception: stops with no code when `## Linter` says none and the user has not chosen to go on.
- `/crav1-complete-task` — Reads one `T#` and the persist rule. Writes the commit-style rule when it is missing. Leaves product code, `spec.md`, push, and the pull request alone in this chat. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` and `crav1-complete-task-agent`.
- `/crav1-complete-tasks` — Reads the `T#` queue on one spec. Writes the commit-style rule once when it is missing. Leaves product code, commits, `spec.md`, push, and the pull request alone in this chat. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` and `crav1-complete-task-agent` once per `T#`.
- `/crav1-complete-features` — Reads ready spec folders already on the default branch. Writes the commit-style rule once when it is missing, and a `feat/<slug>` checkout from default per slug. Leaves product code, commits, `spec.md`, push, and the pull request alone in this chat. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` for that checkout, without re-prompting, and `crav1-complete-task-agent` one `T#` at a time.
  Exception: one ready slug stops and points at `/crav1-complete-tasks` without running it.
- `crav1-complete-task-agent` — Reads one `T#` (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`). Writes that task’s code, `tasks.md`, `verify.md`, `fix-log.md` when a fix runs, and the commits. Leaves `spec.md`, other `T#`s, push, and the pull request alone. Called by `/crav1-complete-task`, `/crav1-complete-tasks`, and `/crav1-complete-features`. Calls `/crav1-implement-task`, `/crav1-verify-spec`, `/crav1-fix-from-verify`, and `/crav1-finalize-commit`.
- `/crav1-verify-spec` — Reads `spec.md`, `tasks.md`, `plan.md`, and the running tree. Writes `verify.md`. Leaves `spec.md` and product code alone. Called by the user and by `crav1-complete-task-agent`. Calls no skill.
  Exception: does not run `/crav1-fix-bug` or `/crav1-review-pr`.
- `/crav1-fix-from-verify` — Reads `verify.md` and the spec folder. Writes the smallest in-spec fix, an appended `fix-log.md`, and that one `verify.md` row when the file exists. Leaves `spec.md` and unimplemented tasks alone. Called by the user and by `crav1-complete-task-agent`. Calls no skill.
  Exception: does not run `/crav1-fix-bug`.
- `/crav1-fix-live` — Reads the same queue as `/crav1-fix-from-verify`. Writes what that skill writes. Leaves `spec.md` alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-fix-from-verify`.
  Exception: prefers live or untested wiring rows.
- `/crav1-feature-branch` — Reads the current branch, the default branch, and whether the tree is dirty. Writes a local checkout of `feat/<slug>` or `spec/<slug>` after the user picks. Leaves commits, push, and the pull request alone. Called by the user, `/crav1-spark-to-spec`, `/crav1-ideas-to-spec`, `/crav1-intake-to-specs`, `/crav1-match-to-specs`, `/crav1-implement-task`, `/crav1-complete-task`, `/crav1-complete-tasks`, and `/crav1-complete-features`. Calls no skill.
  Exception: skips the prompt when there is no repo, no commits, or the branch is already right. A dirty tree does not checkout.
- `/crav1-security-review` — Reads `docs/system/` or a spec that already describes the design, and the change when that is the target. Writes kept findings to `docs/system/security.md` or a Security section on that spec. Leaves code, `plan.md`, and commits alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: spark, plan, and verify do not run it. `/crav1-architecture-reviewer` may name it and does not run it.
- `/crav1-fix-bug` — Reads only the bug the user named and a spec already in front of them. Writes nothing. Leaves code, specs, plans, `verify.md`, and `work-item.md` alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: no bug named, or not a real bug, stops with no lane. Spark, specify, plan, and verify do not run it.
- `/crav1-exploratory-test` — Reads a built slice, `spec.md`, and `plan.md`. Writes bugs in `docs/specs/<slug>/explore.md`. Leaves `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `verify.md`, application code, and the checks the plan already named alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-fix-bug` only when the user says so in that turn.
  Exception: no build of the slice stops with nothing written. The second pass stops at `matched the first pass`, or sooner at `the user said stop`. It does not start Specify, Plan, or Build. It is not a starter option.
- `/crav1-suggest-tests-for-code` — Reads one repo or one area of code that already exists, the tests with that code, and the existing spec. Writes nothing itself. Leaves tests, application code, `plan.md`, and `tasks.md` alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-add-to-spec` for one kept suggestion and for one dismissed suggestion.
  Exception: the whole system, no code pointed at, or no existing spec stops with no list. Leave writes nothing and is offered again. Dismiss is not offered again. It does not start Specify, Plan, or Build. Plan turns a kept suggestion into a task. It is not a starter option.
- `/crav1-meeting-to-specs` — Reads the minutes or transcript after the command, and existing `docs/specs/<slug>/` folders, skipping `_template`. Writes nothing itself. Leaves `docs/system/`, specs, marks, dismissals, and the transcript alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-add-to-spec` for one kept addition.
  Exception: no minutes stops and asks. Dismiss is this run only and is not stored. A kept new feature or bug only names the next command. It does not start Specify, Plan, or Build. It is not a starter option.
- `/crav1-repos-to-spec` — Reads the repos the user named, and `docs/architecture/left-out.md` when that file is there. Writes `docs/architecture/spec.md` when that file is missing, `docs/architecture/left-out.md` for guesses that stay left out, and the `docs/system/` notes `/crav1-explain` reads when those notes are missing. Leaves application code, the next feature, and system notes that are already there alone on the pass that creates the architecture spec. Called by the user and by `/crav1-environment-read` for a confirmed architecture or left-out section. Calls `/crav1-feature-branch` when the destination already has commits.
  Exception: before writing, one question per section (each named repo, inferred guesses, links, left-out) and every item stays listed. A later re-read adds only what is new to the spec and notes, and removes a left-out line when the code shows it or that section dismisses it. A guess stays out until that section accepts it. A link is written only when the code shows it.
- `/crav1-environment-read` — Reads the host the user named, non-prod resources on that host, prod-only resources for shape and connections when the user says yes, and `docs/environments/marks.md` when it exists. After that read, optional SQL metadata and storage structure only when the user says yes. Writes only confirmed lines appended to `docs/environments/marks.md`. Leaves `docs/system`, `docs/architecture/spec.md`, feature specs, `docs/architecture/left-out.md`, and application code alone. Called by the user. Calls `/crav1-keep-current`, `/crav1-repos-to-spec`, and `/crav1-add-to-spec` for the append only after that section is confirmed.
  Exception: does not guess the host. Naming production, prod, or live stops. One pass covers every non-prod environment. Pre-prod, shared-with-prod, and prod-only stay shape and connections until one yes. A no leaves prod-only in Skipped. Look-inside never opens production. A database with no clear environment is asked before it is opened. Missing access stops that look-inside. Never rows, blobs, or production data. Azure, AWS, and Google Cloud each have a reader. Any other host stops with no reader. A fact is seen in that environment. A prod-only line says `prod only`. A link only when the environment shows the connection. Does not start Specify, Plan, or Build. Names `/crav1-pipeline-environments` and does not run it.
- `/crav1-pipeline-environments` — Reads Azure DevOps pipeline definitions for the org and project the user named, and `docs/environments/marks.md` when it exists. Writes only confirmed lines appended to `docs/environments/marks.md`. Leaves `docs/system`, `docs/architecture/spec.md`, feature specs, `docs/architecture/left-out.md`, and application code alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: Azure DevOps, the org, or the project missing stops the read. A missing CLI, extension, or login stops it. It does not run a pipeline. It names `/crav1-environment-read` and does not run it. It is not a starter option.
- `/crav1-explain` — Reads the `docs/system/` notes spark, ideas, intake, or match already wrote. Writes a short TLDR in the chat, one level deeper only when asked, and one part when pointed at. Leaves specs, code, and the picture alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: does not guess, invent a second document, teach, or start Specify, Plan, or Build. When the picture is older than the specs, it names `/crav1-keep-current` and does not run it.
- `/crav1-whats-known-about` — Reads one name, a sentence or two, an `@` path, or a focus, then the matching spec, plan, tasks, Match, and open questions, plus `docs/system/`, `docs/architecture/spec.md`, and `docs/environments/marks.md`. After that, reads Azure resource settings and recent changes, and Azure DevOps work items, open pull requests, and branches. Writes nothing. Leaves specs, code, marks, commits, and pull requests alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: pasted minutes or a long dump stops and names `/crav1-meeting-to-specs` or `/crav1-match-dump-to-specs`. Two or more close hits ask which. A live-read failure offers Retry or Skip. It does not start Specify, Plan, or Build. It is not a starter option.
- `/crav1-keep-current` — Reads the picture and what a spec already states. Writes new lines on the short description, the context diagram, and how the parts connect. Leaves existing picture lines, glossary rows, design, and build alone. Called by the user and by `/crav1-environment-read` for a confirmed system section. Calls no skill.
  Exception: spark, ideas, intake, match, match-dump, and code-into-specs run this picture update on the pass that appends a glossary row.
- `/crav1-export-spec` — Reads `spec.md` and the ideas-to-spec format recipes. Writes only the requested files under `export/`. Leaves `spec.md` and application code alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
- `/crav1-draft-commit-message` — Reads the staged or unstaged diff, recent `git log`, an existing persist rule, and `work-item.md` when it exists. Writes a host persist rule only when the user chooses onward. Leaves the git commit alone. Called by the user and by `/crav1-finalize-commit`. Calls no skill.
  Exception: commits only when the user also asked to commit in that turn.
- `/crav1-finalize-commit` — Reads the same commit inputs through draft. Writes the persist rule when onward is chosen, and the git commit when the user picks commit. Leaves push alone. Called by the user and by `crav1-complete-task-agent`. Calls `/crav1-draft-commit-message`.
  Exception: the worker commits immediately and skips the menu.
- `/crav1-open-pr` — Reads the change branch, the spec folder, `verify.md`, and `work-item.md` when it exists. Writes one pull request after an explicit yes to push. Leaves new commits and the merge alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: names `/crav1-review-pr` and `/crav1-merge-pr` and does not run them.
- `/crav1-review-pr` — Reads one named open pull request, its diff, the spec, the plan, `verify.md`, the body, and the required linter. Writes nothing. Leaves code, the spec, the plan, comments, and the merge alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: spark, specify, verify, `/crav1-open-pr`, and `/crav1-merge-pr` do not run it.
- `/crav1-merge-pr` — Reads one named pull request. Writes a merge commit on the host, and fast-forwards local default when the tree is clean after a confirmed two-parent merge. Leaves squash, rebase, branch deletion, and work-item links alone. Called by the user. Calls no skill.
  Exception: a required red host check stops it. It does not run `/crav1-review-pr`.
